<!-- formalization -->

**Theorem (`ApproximableMap.exists_rel_of_subset_image`).** If every token of a finite set $Y$ arises from some approximable input under an element $x$, then some single consistent input under $x$ relates to the whole of $Y$.

*Proof.* Empty $Y$ uses the empty relation after weakening; the inductive step joins the witnesses for the new token and the remainder via right-union and monotonicity. □

**Definition (`ApproximableMap.toElement`).** The element map of an approximable mapping $f$ sends an element $x$ of the source to the element of the target whose tokens are those $Y$ for which some finite input under $x$ relates to $\{Y\}$.

**Theorem (`ApproximableMap.mem_toElement`).** Membership in the carrier of the element map is exactly the witnessing relation of the definition.

*Proof.* Unfolding. □

**Theorem (`ApproximableMap.toElement_mono`).** The element map is monotone.

*Proof.* A witnessing input under a smaller element remains under a larger one. □

**Theorem (`ApproximableMap.rel_iff_closure_le`).** Consistent sets $u$ and $v$ are related by an approximable mapping if and only if the closure of $v$ approximates the image of the closure of $u$.

*Proof.* Relatedness yields singleton witnesses under the left closure; conversely a relational witness under the left closure is weakened back to $u$ and $v$ by monotonicity. □

**Theorem (`ApproximableMap.le_iff_toElement_le`).** One approximable mapping lies below another if and only if its element map approximates the other’s at every source element.

*Proof.* Pointwise comparison of images preserves relational witnesses; conversely the closure characterization transfers a related pair through the pointwise inequality. □

**Theorem (`ApproximableMap.ext_iff_toElement`).** Two approximable mappings are equal if and only if they agree as element maps on every source element.

*Proof.* Equality of maps yields pointwise equality of images; conversely mutual pointwise order via the order characterization forces equal relations. □
